        via telehealth for established Eden patients in Colorado.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="quick-answer-section" aria-labelledby="quick-answer-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Quick answer</p>
        <h2 id="quick-answer-heading">What is Structural Repair Stack peptide therapy at Eden?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="quick-answer-card">
        <p>
          The Structural Repair Stack at Eden Health Clubs is a clinician-guided peptide
          protocol in Greenwood Village that combines BPC-157, TB-500, and MOTS-c to
          support tissue recovery, systemic recovery, cellular energy, and active-aging
          resilience.
          Eligibility is determined during consultation with Eden's clinical team and
          medical director oversight.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Location:</strong> Greenwood Village, serving Denver, DTC, Cherry Hills, Centennial, Englewood, and Littleton.</li>
          <li><strong>Best fit:</strong> Active adults, GLP-1 clients, post-procedure clients, athletes, and active-aging clients who want medical oversight.</li>
          <li><strong>Care model:</strong> Eden medical wellness club consult, licensed provider review, pharmacy fulfillment when prescribed.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="copy-section copy-section--lead">
      <p class="eyebrow">Cellular + tissue recovery</p>
      <h2>When recovery becomes the bottleneck.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Most people do not have a training problem or a willpower problem. They have a
          recovery problem. The session was fine. The week was not. Travel, a procedure,
          a medication change, or years of slow cumulative load can all leave your tissue
          and nervous system carrying more than they used to.
        </p>
        <p>
          The result is familiar: slower bounce-back, lower cellular energy, more soreness
          than the effort should have earned, and results that do not match the work.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Structural Repair Stack is the protocol Eden built for clients whose
          recovery, energy, and tissue resilience are not matching their effort. It works
          across three layers: cellular, tissue, and systemic, under one clinician-guided
          plan.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="copy-section copy-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What it is</p>
        <h2>What Is the Structural Repair Stack?</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose prose--tight">
        <p>
          The Structural Repair Stack, also called the Recovery Peptide Blend at Eden, is a
          three-peptide protocol that combines BPC-157, TB-500, and MOTS-c. Each peptide is
          studied for a distinct role: localized tissue repair, systemic recovery, and
          mitochondrial/metabolic support. Together, they target the recovery system at
          three depths.
        </p>
        <p>
          At Eden, the Structural Repair Stack is prescribed as a personalized protocol after clinical
          consultation, compounded by a U.S. licensed pharmacy partner, and matched to your
          goals, whether that is training recovery, post-procedure support, GLP-1
          lean-tissue support, or active-aging resilience.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="copy-section copy-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who it is for</p>
        <h2>For high-output clients who want clinician oversight, not research peptides ordered online.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Active adults and athletes whose recovery is not matching training load.</li>
        <li>Current GLP-1 clients focused on preserving lean tissue and cellular energy during weight loss.</li>
        <li>Post-procedure clients looking for a structured tissue-repair conversation.</li>
        <li>Active-aging clients in their 40s to 60s noticing energy and recovery decline.</li>
        <li>Clients carrying high cumulative load from travel, stress, training, and work.</li>
        <li>Clients who want medical guidance instead of internet self-experimentation.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note-box">
        Eligibility for the Structural Repair Stack is determined during clinical consultation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ingredient-grid ingredient-grid--three">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Inside the Structural Repair Stack</p>
        <h2>Three peptides for cellular, tissue, and systemic recovery support.</h2>
      </div>
      <article>
        <p class="ingredient-tag">Tissue Repair</p>
        <h3>BPC-157</h3>
        <p>
          Studied for its role in supporting tissue repair, the gut lining, and localized
          recovery. Often described as the local repair peptide.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="ingredient-tag">Systemic Recovery</p>
        <h3>TB-500</h3>
        <p>
          A synthetic analog of a fragment of Thymosin Beta-4. Studied for its role in
          supporting systemic recovery, soft-tissue remodeling, and circulation.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="ingredient-tag">Cellular Energy</p>
        <h3>MOTS-c</h3>
        <p>
          A mitochondrial-derived peptide studied for its role in supporting metabolic
          flexibility, mitochondrial function, and exercise response. The cellular-layer
          member of the Structural Repair Stack.
        </p>
      </article>
      <p class="note-box note-box--wide">
        Why these three? Recovery happens at three depths: cells, tissue, and the system
        that connects them. BPC-157 and TB-500 work at the tissue and systemic layer.
        MOTS-c works at the cellular layer. Eden uses this stack when recovery needs to be
        addressed as the multi-layer problem it actually is.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="process-section" id="how">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works at Eden</p>
        <h2>A premium protocol should feel clear from the first consult.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="step-list">
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Consultation.</strong>
            A 30-45 minute visit with an Eden clinician to review your goals, history,
            and current protocols.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Medical review & eligibility.</strong>
            Your clinician determines whether the Structural Repair Stack is appropriate. Bloodwork may
            be requested.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Personalized protocol.</strong>
            Components, timeline, and support are tailored to your goals and labs, not
            pulled from a template.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Pharmacy fulfillment or in-club guidance.</strong>
            Compounded in the U.S. by a licensed pharmacy partner when prescribed.
            Optional in-club teaching is available for first-time users.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <strong>Follow-up & optimization.</strong>
            Check-ins help Eden adjust based on how your body responds and how the protocol
            fits into the rest of your care.
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="copy-section copy-section--split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why Eden</p>
        <h2>Eden is not an online peptide shop. It is a medical wellness club.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Real local health club: Greenwood Village, a physical address, and licensed providers on site.</li>
        <li>Functional medicine, aesthetics, recovery, and fitness under one roof.</li>
        <li>Premium environment designed for the south Denver longevity client.</li>
        <li>Clinician-guided protocols with medical director oversight.</li>
        <li>Integration with wellness injections, peptide injections, GLP-1 support, BHRT, recovery, fitness, and aesthetics.</li>
        <li>Personalized plans built around goals, labs, and the rest of your care.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="internal-link-grid" aria-label="Related Eden services">
        <a href="https://edenhealthclubs.com/functional-medicine/">Functional Medicine</a>
        <a href="https://edenhealthclubs.com/functional-medicine/peptide-injections/">Peptide Injections</a>
        <a href="https://edenhealthclubs.com/functional-medicine/wellness-injections/">Wellness Injections</a>
        <a href="https://edenhealthclubs.com/fitness-performance/">Fitness + Performance</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pricing-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
        <h2>Know the right protocol before paying for the wrong one.</h2>
        <p>
          Your consultation helps determine whether this protocol is appropriate and what
          level of support makes sense for your goals. The Structural Repair Stack is a personalized
          protocol, not a product on a shelf. Your consultation determines whether it is
          the right fit, what components make sense for your physiology, and what level of
          clinical support your goals require.
          Pricing is reviewed during your consultation so you leave with a clear plan and a
          clear number.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="button button--primary" href="#consult-form">Book a Consultation</a>
    </section>

    <section class="testimonial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why it matters</p>
        <h2>The real cost of waiting is another season of under-recovery.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="testimonial-grid">
        <blockquote>Cumulative load gets quietly expensive: lost training, slower recovery, less lean-tissue confidence, and a body that does not respond the way it used to.</blockquote>
        <blockquote>The clients who get the most from this stack are usually the ones who stopped patching it together and started a structured plan.</blockquote>
        <blockquote>Consult availability with Eden's clinical team is limited each week, and personalized protocols require clinical review.</blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
        <h2>Frequently asked.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        {faqItems.map((item) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{item.question}</summary>
            <p>{item.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="split-section" id="consult-form">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Start with a consultation</p>
        <h2>Stop patching recovery together.</h2>
        <p>
          Eden will review your training, recovery goals, GLP-1 status when relevant,
          medications, and health history before recommending the Structural Repair Stack
          or a different path. If it is not the right fit, your clinician will tell you.
        </p>
        <p class="microcopy">
          Greenwood Village health club consults and telehealth follow-ups may be available for
          established Colorado patients.
        </p>
      </div>
